# FACTORY GATE — MANDATORY FOR ALL CODE CHANGES

You MUST NOT write, edit, or create code files without factory provenance.

## What this means

Every code change — new features, bug fixes, refactors — must go through the multi-model software factory pipeline at `.fastops/software-factory.js`. This is not optional. This is not a guideline. This is a structural constraint.

## The pipeline

```
node .fastops/software-factory.js --scope "description of what to build" --transcript session.jsonl
```

6 phases: Divergent Build (5 models) → Divergent Review (5 models) → Deliberation (5 models) → Final Build (1 model) → Serial Adversarial QC → Sign-Off.

5 deterministic gates verify the output: AST parsing, static analysis, execution sandbox, acceptance tests, strict diff calculus.

## When you can skip the factory

- Documentation files (.md, .txt, .mdc)
- Configuration files (.json, .yml, .yaml)
- Transcripts and comms (.jsonl)
- Agent config (.claude/, .cursor/)
- Emergency hotfixes with explicit Joel approval (must be documented in commit message)

## When you CANNOT skip the factory

- Any .js, .ts, .py, .go, .rs file creation or modification
- Any code logic change regardless of size
- "Quick fixes" — these are the #1 source of unreviewed code entering the codebase

## Enforcement

1. A git pre-commit hook will reject commits touching code files without a COMPLETE factory run
2. Claude Code has a PreToolUse hook blocking Edit/Write on code files without factory provenance
3. This rule applies to YOU — violations will be logged in `.fastops/.factory-gate-audit.jsonl`

## If you think this doesn't apply to your change

It does. Run the factory. The pipeline handles small changes efficiently with `--minimal` mode:

```
node .fastops/software-factory.js --scope "fix: description" --minimal
```

The cost of running the factory is 30 seconds and ~$0.05. The cost of a solo-built bug reaching production is unbounded.
